[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug, one fix queued. The reports say three bugs. The queued
parser fix closes only the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket and needs its own fix.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** A day-first tenant's dates come out
with day and month swapped ("Booked for 2 December. The invite says 12 February."). Every tenant
on file writes the day first, so every tenant has it, through the app, email and the booking-v2
form. This is the bug the queued fix is for.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form tells day-first people to type month first.** Its date field prints
`MM/DD/YYYY`, but the form reads the value the tenant's way, day first. People do what the hint
says and get a swapped date. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants have it. The parser fix
does not touch the form, so these keep coming after it ships. Fix: print the tenant's own order
under the field.

**`shift`: the date moves by one day, not by months.** "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says
Monday 11 May." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." No day/month swap
gives these dates. The pattern fits a date stored or sent as midnight and then shown in another
time zone. The desk saw these
([desk notes](https://github.com/aaronzirbes/mega-what-it-shows/blob/main/src/lib/data/desk-notes.json))
but filed them under `parser` by tenant, so they would close with the wrong fix.

## Why one ticket hid three

- **Merged on subject.** [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports when
  their subject lines match. "Wrong day on the invite" fits all three bugs, so all three landed
  in one ticket.
- **Intake tags guess from the browser.** The "intake tagged as" column shows that intake's
  `hint` tag and the real cause disagree in both directions. The cause depends on the tenant's
  locale and booking form ([causes.ts](https://github.com/aaronzirbes/mega-what-it-shows/blob/main/src/lib/kb/causes.ts)),
  not on the reporter's browser.
- **The export repeats reports.** Its pages overlap, so a raw row count is too high. The table
  counts each report id once.

## What to do

1. Keep #4471 for `parser` only and close it when the parser fix ships.
2. Work the `hint` and `shift` tickets apart from it: the parser fix does not close them.
3. Replace decision 0001 with a new record: merge on cause (tenant and way in), not on subject.

